        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Publications: Woman's Day, The Lady, Beyond Black & White, Ebony, Jet, Reuters\n- Companies: The Great Atlantic & Pacific Tea Company, Hearst Corporation\n- People: Christelyn Karazin\n- Places: Britain, London\n\nFacts:\n- The Lady has been in continuous publication since 1885 and is based in London.\n- Woman's Day was first published in 1931 by The Great Atlantic & Pacific Tea Company.\n- The Lady is Britain's longest-running weekly women's magazine.\n- Hearst Corporation is the current publisher of Woman's Day.\n- Christelyn Karazin hosts the blog Beyond Black & White.\n- Christelyn Karazin has written for Woman's Day, Ebony, Jet, and Reuters.",
